WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.310 --> 00:00:05.378
- So, I, um, got some shock cord like this,

00:00:05.378 --> 00:00:09.419
and laboriously cut
all the covering off it

00:00:09.419 --> 00:00:12.219
to expose the natural rubber.

00:00:12.219 --> 00:00:13.837
And here's the bungee.

00:00:13.837 --> 00:00:16.170
We had this old potato sack,

00:00:17.068 --> 00:00:18.779
and I filled it up with rocks

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:20.917
and dropped it over the side

00:00:20.917 --> 00:00:24.230
and it just hit the water, split,

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:28.025
dropping all the stones,
and that was our test.

00:00:28.025 --> 00:00:30.099
So I thought, well, we're
not doing one more test

00:00:30.099 --> 00:00:31.135
it's gonna be me.

00:00:31.135 --> 00:00:33.195
(laughing)

00:00:33.195 --> 00:00:36.176
And I hit the water, (bleep), so hard.

00:00:36.176 --> 00:00:37.221
Bang!

00:00:37.221 --> 00:00:38.830
Right in over my head.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:40.898
And I thought, well that's it.

00:00:40.898 --> 00:00:44.629
And then all of a sudden,
I'm out of the water again.

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:46.879
And I'm thinking: “It works!”

00:00:48.049 --> 00:00:50.540
And that was the first modern bungee jump.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.173
That was the start of things to come.

00:00:52.173 --> 00:00:54.506
(long beep)

00:00:55.614 --> 00:00:57.034
- [Man] Heads up!

00:00:57.034 --> 00:00:59.867
(edgy rock music)

00:01:11.659 --> 00:01:14.056
- Our weekends were pretty
much taken up with bungee.

00:01:14.056 --> 00:01:16.426
Different places, different crew.

00:01:16.426 --> 00:01:17.472
(laughing)

00:01:17.472 --> 00:01:21.140
I teamed up with AJ, and he
was of a like-mind like me.

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:23.687
Newtonian physics had been
thrown out the window.

00:01:23.687 --> 00:01:24.879
- Just carry on.

00:01:24.879 --> 00:01:28.438
- And we had thoughts very, very quickly.

00:01:28.438 --> 00:01:30.205
And of course, every bridge was getting

00:01:30.205 --> 00:01:34.372
bigger and bigger and bigger
and that was exciting.

00:01:40.527 --> 00:01:43.028
My dream was going out to sea so we said,

00:01:43.028 --> 00:01:45.217
we better jump the Auckland Harbor Bridge.

00:01:45.217 --> 00:01:47.162
So we drive up onto the bridge,

00:01:47.162 --> 00:01:49.571
everyone jump out with
their little bits and pieces

00:01:49.571 --> 00:01:52.706
down underneath the bridge,
and we're ready to go.

00:01:52.706 --> 00:01:55.217
- [Man] Looks like the Deodar's
coming for a visit, folks.

00:01:55.217 --> 00:01:58.716
- What the police said was,
"Whatever you're gonna do,

00:01:58.716 --> 00:02:01.343
don't do it!"

00:02:01.343 --> 00:02:05.808
AJ turns to me, he goes,
"Did you hear that?"

00:02:05.808 --> 00:02:07.512
And I went, "No."

00:02:07.512 --> 00:02:08.893
(laughing)

00:02:08.893 --> 00:02:10.757
Yeah, we just jumped.

00:02:10.757 --> 00:02:14.859
(playful, inspiring music)

00:02:14.859 --> 00:02:17.109
(cheering)

00:02:18.766 --> 00:02:20.533
I just went and there
was this lone policeman

00:02:20.533 --> 00:02:23.710
on the back of the Deodar with
his mouth just gaping open.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:26.392
- [Man] AJ, you can forget
your trip to Europe, son.

00:02:26.392 --> 00:02:29.026
Then the story broke, and then it was

00:02:29.026 --> 00:02:31.026
guns blazing after that.

00:02:33.239 --> 00:02:35.718
AJ went overseas and ended up doing some

00:02:35.718 --> 00:02:39.885
bungee jumping over there,
we kind of drifted apart.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:43.293
I didn't really get a good handle on

00:02:43.293 --> 00:02:46.126
how commercial it was going to be.

00:02:47.814 --> 00:02:51.327
I was just really testing the idea.

00:02:51.327 --> 00:02:54.910
(playful, inspiring music)

